<header class="sp-head"><a class="sp-portrait" href="/encyclopedia/patrice-lumumba" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patrice-lumumba.jpg" alt="" width="104" height="104"></a><p class="featured-region">30 June 1960 · Léopoldville</p><h1 class="sp-title">Lumumba's Independence Day Speech</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrice-lumumba">Patrice Lumumba</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>At the ceremony granting independence to the Belgian Congo, King Baudouin praised the 'genius' of his great-granduncle Leopold II, whose Congo Free State had been notorious for its atrocities, and President Joseph Kasa-Vubu replied with conciliatory words. Then Patrice Lumumba, the new prime minister, who was not on the programme, rose and answered the king with an account of what colonial rule had meant for the Congolese.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>We have known sarcasm, insults and blows that we had to endure morning, noon and night, because we were Black.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">Speech at the independence ceremony, Léopoldville, 30 June 1960, translated from the French.</p><div class="sp-full"><button type="button" class="sp-share" data-share-text="“We have known sarcasm, insults and blows that we had to endure morning, noon and night, because we were Black.” — Patrice Lumumba, Lumumba's Independence Day Speech" data-share-img="/images/og/speech-lumumba-independence-day-speech.jpg">Share this quote</button></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>Within days the army mutinied against its Belgian officers, Belgium sent troops, and the mineral-rich province of Katanga seceded with Belgian backing, beginning the Congo Crisis. Lumumba appealed to the United Nations and then to the Soviet Union; he was dismissed in September, arrested, and in January 1961 handed over to his enemies in Katanga and murdered. Belgium later acknowledged a moral responsibility for his death.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-crisis">Congo Crisis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/katanga">Katanga</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mobutu-sese-seko">Mobutu Sese Seko</a></div></div></section>
